# Every `FilingPeriod` this pack has, in order — the real, silent
# prerequisite Plan 107 Slice 4's console picker needs: `period-summary`/
# `period-diff`/`period-history` (Slices 1-3) each take a period as
# input, none lists which ones exist.
#
# **No caller-supplied placeholder at all** — unlike every other query in
# this pack, this one takes no bindings, matching `run_pack_query`'s
# already-supported empty-bindings case.
#
# CAUTION for whoever edits this file: `placeholder_names` (the
# `graph-owl-api` function that finds a registered query's required
# bindings) scans the *whole* query text, comments included — writing a
# double-brace placeholder form in a comment, even descriptively, demands
# that binding here too. This has now bitten `period-summary.sparql`,
# `period-diff.sparql`, and this file — avoid double braces in prose
# entirely across every query in this pack.

PREFIX gst: <https://graph-owl.dev/packs/gst#>

SELECT ?period ?periodLabel WHERE {
  GRAPH ?g {
    ?period a gst:FilingPeriod ;
            gst:period ?periodLabel .
  }
}
ORDER BY ?periodLabel
